  "vulnerability_information": "###  **Vulnerable Website URL or Application:**\n\n```\n█████\n\n```\n\n---\n\n###  **Description of Security Issue:**\n\nThe SSL VPN endpoint exposed at the above IP address is vulnerable to **Reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)** via the `user` parameter.\n\nThis issue corresponds to **CVE-2025-0133**, which allows an unauthenticated attacker to inject and execute arbitrary JavaScript in the browser of a victim who clicks on a maliciously crafted link.\n\nSuccessful exploitation may lead to:\n\n* Session hijacking\n* Credential theft\n* Browser-based exploits\n\nThis vulnerability poses a serious risk when combined with phishing or social engineering attacks.\n\n---\n\n### **Exploit Scenario:**\n\nAn attacker crafts a malicious link to the VPN endpoint, injecting JavaScript in the `user` parameter. If a user with access to the VPN portal clicks the link, the injected code will be executed in their browser.\n\n\nOnce opened by a victim, the script will execute immediately, demonstrating the vulnerability.\n\n---\n###  **Steps to Reproduce Bug:**\n\n1. Open the following URL in a browser:\n\n```\n███\n\n```\n\n2. Observe that the browser executes the JavaScript payload (a `prompt` popup appears), indicating an XSS vulnerability.\n\n3. Confirm that the `user` parameter is reflected unsanitized into the response.\n\n---\n##POC:\n█████████\n\n## Impact\n\nThis reflected **Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)** vulnerability can lead to **critical security risks**, especially since it affects a **Fortinet SSL VPN endpoint** — a commonly targeted enterprise asset.\n\n## System Host(s)\n█████\n\n## Affected Product(s) and Version(s)\n\n\n## CVE Numbers\nCVE-2025-0133\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n1. Open the following URL in a browser:\n\n```\n█████\n\n```\n\n2. Observe that the browser executes the JavaScript payload (a `prompt` popup appears), indicating an XSS vulnerability.\n\n3. Confirm that the `user` parameter is reflected unsanitized into the response.\n\n## Suggested Mitigation/Remediation Actions\n\n\n",
